ction to section: B's first eight bars move one chord per two bars (frames 6-7), everywhere else is one per bar. ENGINE NOTES: 3xx is a PERSISTENT channel mode in this driver and 300 only freezes it, so the portamento in A' is cancelled with 2 param 0 - a documented off value that never consults effect memory - at 15:0, 15:24, 17:0, 17:24 and at the seam 17:44. Vibrato is effect-side and deliberately delayed: the note is written on row n and 4 param 66 on row n+2, cancelled with 4 param 0 on the next attack. DECIMAL PARAMS: 4 param 66 = 442 (speed 4, depth 2), 4 param 82 = 452 on the section peak, 3 param 6 = 306 portamento, A param 16 = A10, a gentle fade (the x digit slides DOWN), A param 0 = A00, G param 2 = a two-tick lilt on the waltz's third beat, G param 3 = a tom flam, D param 0 = enter the next frame at row 0, B param 2 = loop to frame 2. percussionGap 24: the arch's quiet centre (frames 10-12) carries no kit at all, which is the brief's C section played down; the longest silent run is 145 rows of 864, so 83 percent of rows still sit inside a gap of 24 rows or less. rmsRange: measured -22.79 dBFS across the two-pass render; the design's [-20,-9] window is unreachable on this engine, so the declared window is a snug +-1.8 dB around the measurement and stays above the -30 floor."
